<title>USA: Fed's Greenspan sees global benefits from EMU.</title>
<headline>Fed's Greenspan sees global benefits from EMU.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan on Wednesday said European success in achieving Economic and Monetary Union would benefit both Europe and the world economy.</p>
<p>&quot;To the extent it enhances Europe's ability to become an effective world competitor, it's going to help us,&quot; the U.S. central bank chief told the Senate Banking Committee. &quot;We hope that the struggles they are (having) -- which are obviously considerable -- bring fruition.&quot;</p>
</text>
